Real trained ML forecast model — trains a regression model on actual
historical price data (via yfinance) to predict future price movement,
replacing the illustrative EMA/linear/Monte Carlo math with something
genuinely fit to data and evaluated on a held-out test set.


Model: Gradient Boosting Regressor predicting next-day return, using
engineered features (lagged returns, moving averages, volatility, RSI).
Forecasts are generated by predicting one step ahead, applying that
return, then feeding the result back in to predict the next step
(a walk-forward projection).

IMPORTANT: This is still a simple, honestly-evaluated model for a
learning project — not a production trading signal. Its test-set R^2
and directional accuracy are reported transparently precisely so you
don't overstate what it can actually do. Markets are extremely hard
to predict; a model with modest but positive directional accuracy on
held-out data is a reasonable, defensible result for this project.




